>I believe an author does have a moral right (and a copyright) to
>restrict reposting. When notice is given, it should be respected.

The default status for a work under current copyright law is that it is
copyrighted unless there a disclaimer that those rights are given up.
There doesn't need to be a copyright notice on something for the
copyright to be valid.

It is a rather simple concept: if you didn't write it, and the author
hasn't told you that you do, you don't have the rights the author has 
to the material.


